WEBVTT
Language: en

NOTE
Voiced by Tello (Kokoro af_heart). V4 narration — free-home story, Nov 2026.

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:02.360
Your first inspection, without guessing.

00:00:03.070 --> 00:00:07.810
This is Title22, for California RCFE and ARF owners.

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.180
Nobody hands a new administrator the list.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.760
Staff files, the 40-hour training, clearance dates, incident reports.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.780
They live in binders until a page goes missing.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:24.660
Open Title22.app and tap create your account.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.800
Your dashboard shows what's missing.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.460
Ask Tello to check it for DSS gaps.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:36.320
One menu holds staff, training, the checklist, documents, and the audit log.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.260
The checklist puts overdue items on top and prints as a report.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:43.820
Add staff once.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:46.910
An expired certificate shows the name and the date.

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:52.110
Invite your team by role, including read-only access for an inspector.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:58.010
Title22 loads the requirements and puts your own dates against them.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.500
Every alert names a person and a date.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:02.980
Your readiness score climbs as you work.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:06.060
Shown here, the practice home with invented staff.

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:08.870
Setup is an evening.

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:11.380
Add your staff, enter each date once.

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:14.010
Then it warns you before DSS does.

00:01:15.490 --> 00:01:18.200
Every module maps to something an analyst checks.

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:30.310
LIC 622 staff files, 40-hour training, clearance alerts, a DSS readiness checklist, a document vault, and LIC 624 incident reports.

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:41.450
The core app holds staff records only — no resident records, no medications. Medication records live apart, in their own corner, under a signed BAA.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:46.530
Tello, the AI compliance assistant, briefs you every morning.

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:51.380
It flags overdue tasks, expiring certifications, and missing documents.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.800
And it never comments on clinical dosage on any plan.

00:01:56.310 --> 00:01:59.400
Each facility's records are walled off at the database.

00:01:59.830 --> 00:02:04.160
Role-based access, no shared logins, and an append-only audit trail.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.300
Export your records anytime.

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:16.110
Requirements are guided by a certified California RCFE administrator, and grounded in the Title 22 regulation text.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.140
Title22 helps you close gaps.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:22.140
Staying licensed is still the facility's job.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:36.890
Your first home is free — no clock, no card — and it stays free. Packages with staff training: $29 a month for one home, $79 for two to five, $139 for six or more.

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:42.390
Every new account gets 30 days of full access. No card, nothing to cancel.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:49.130
When it ends, your home stays on the free plan — nothing taken away or locked. Only the training pauses.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.770
Built for new owners, CE and ICTP trainers, and compliance consultants.

00:02:56.170 --> 00:02:59.050
Start with your free home at title22.app.

00:02:59.350 --> 00:03:00.390
Just an email.

00:03:00.690 --> 00:03:03.080
A practice home is ready the moment you're in.
